General_SiSo_Auto_Verification_of_UP_fragmentation_DL_UL
    [Documentation]     The purpose of the test is to check if the activation of Uplink & Downlink UP dynamic
    ...                 fragmentation is working properly.
    ...                 The test case is responsible for checking messages in BTSlog files and Journal files in snapshot
    ...                 for Uplink and Downlink after performing parallel L3 call with data transfer.
    ...                 The test case fails after checking all the messages if at least one message is not in BTSlog
    ...                 files or Journal files.
    ...                 To properly execute this keyword you should have configured:
    ...                     1) at least 2 UEs in your testline and init file,
    ...                     2) proper parameters in scf or delta file to launch UP Fragmentation
    ...                        (you can find preconditions parameters in QC test description),
    ...                     3) required flags in swconfig.txt for capturing syslog messages:
    ...                         #SYSLOG severity prints
    ...                         0x10040=1
    ...                         #SYSLOG severity prints
    ...                         0x1003F=1
    ...                     4) additional flags in swconfig.txt until they are not switched on automatically
    ...                        for CB008941 (not applicable since May 2023):
    ...                         0x600012=1 #CB8941 BOAM_NRTS
    ...                         0x190297=1 #CB8941 BOAM_RUMAG
    ...                         0x190305=1 # CB8941 BOAM_RUMAG UL (default enabled)
    ...                         0x190306=1 # CB8941 BOAM_RUMAG DL(default enabled)
    ...                         0x600017=1 #CB8941 BOAM_NRTS_rdUlUpFragmentation ---> UL muting
    ...                         0x600018=1 #CB8941 BOAM_NRTS_rdDlUpFragmentation ---> DL muting
    ...                 ARGS:
    ...                 - called_cells: list of configuration distnames of cells to be called; defaults to None.
    ...                             Example: ['MRBTS-50163/NRBTS-55196/NRCELL-0', 'MRBTS-50163/NRBTS-55196/NRCELL-1']
    ...                 - duration: duration of data transfer test in seconds i.e. 30s; defaults to 60s.
    ...                 - protocol: data transfer protocol; defaults to UDP.
    ...                 - udp_buffer: monitoring data buffer; defaults to 4M.
    ...                 - ue_network_modes: dict with UE serial numbers and desired network modes e.g. {"SN1234": "NR_only"}
    ...                                     possible UE network modes: NR_only, LTE_only, NR_LTE
    ...                                     when using more than one UE please make sure that the modes you choose are either all
    ...                                     with "_only" suffix or all "NR_LTE" as it is not yet possible to mix those.
    ...                                     mandatory for SA+NSA setups, defaults to None
    ...                 - throughputs: dict with throughput and deviation values for each cell identified by
    ...                         it's nrCellIdentity for NR cells, eutranCellId for LTE cells, wnCelId for WCDMA cells.
    ...                             Example:
    ...                             {
    ...                                 '827736065':
    ...                                      {
    ...                                          'throughput':
    ...                                              {
    ...                                                  'downlink': '100 Mbits/sec',
    ...                                                  'uplink': '15 Mbits/sec'
    ...                                              },
    ...                                          'deviation': '80%'
    ...                                      },
    ...                             }

