Private Is matching string in syslog
    [Arguments]                                         ${string_to_find}
    ...                                                 ${syslog_dir}
    [Documentation]     Checks if given string appeared in locally stored syslog. Syslog dir should only contain logs
    ...                 to be checked. Returns True if custom string is found in files, None otherwise.
    ...                 :param string_to_find:  string to appear in syslog
    ...                 :type string_to_find: str
    ...                 :param syslog_dir:  path to dir where syslog file is stored
    ...                 :type syslog_dir: str
    ...                 :return: True if custom string is found in files, None otherwise
    ...                 :rtype: bool/None
    ${is_string_found}=                                 Run Keyword And Continue On Failure
    ...                                                 btslog_parser.verify_if_custom_string_exists_in_custom_log_directory
    ...                                                 custom_str=${string_to_find}
    ...                                                 custom_log_path=${syslog_dir}
    Run Keyword If                                      ${is_string_found}
    ...                                                 Robot Log Operation
    ...                                                 "${string_to_find}" is in BTSlog/Journal - Success!
    ...                                                 ELSE
    ...                                                 Robot Log Operation
    ...                                                 "${string_to_find}" is not in BTSlog/Journal - Error!
    [Return]                                            ${is_string_found}

